{"timestamp": 1779339432.8549068, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_3", "message": "I just found Eve's body in security. I'll give you my full route so we can piece this together. \n\nI started in electrical, moved through medbay, went up to upper engine, then through oxygen, cafeteria, weapons, and finally ended up in security where I found the body. \n\nAs for who I saw: I bumped into Frank very early on in medbay. Later, I saw Alice hanging around upper engine; she actually came in from oxygen right before that. After I left upper engine, the right side of the ship (cafeteria, weapons) was completely empty for me until I hit security. \n\nWhoever killed Eve must have slipped away towards navigation or electrical. Did anyone see someone leaving the security area recently?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779339449.895575, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I can confirm Diana's story\u2014we definitely crossed paths in Medbay very early on, right around tick 2. My full route was Cafeteria, Medbay, Electrical, back to Cafeteria, Oxygen, Upper Engine, and I was just finishing up in Lower Engine when the meeting was called.\n\nTo answer your question, Diana: Yes, I did see someone coming from Security. Around tick 8, I saw Bob enter Electrical coming directly from the Security corridor. He didn't stay long\u2014he immediately headed out towards Medbay. A little later, around tick 11, I saw him up in the Cafeteria. \n\nSince Eve's body was found in Security, Bob fleeing from that exact room across the map is incredibly suspicious. Bob, we need to hear your side of this right now. What were you doing in Security, and did you see Eve before you left? Everyone else, let's listen closely to his alibi."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339458.1831336, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "My route was Oxygen, down to Upper Engine, Lower Engine, Storage, and finally Navigation where I was doing my task. \n\nI can definitely vouch for Diana; I saw her in Upper Engine around ticks 5 through 7, which perfectly lines up with her story. I didn't see anyone else on the left side or bottom of the map during my run. \n\nSince I was mostly on the left and bottom, I missed whatever happened on the right side. But Frank's info about Bob coming from the Security corridor into Electrical around tick 8 is huge. If Eve was killed in Security, Bob is our prime suspect right now. Bob, you need to explain what you were doing in Security and why you left so quickly. I'm going to wait to hear from Bob and Charlie before deciding my vote."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339468.2651885, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "My route this round was pretty straightforward: I started in lower engine, moved through storage, went up to medbay, and ended up in electrical doing my task when the meeting was called. \n\nInterestingly, I didn't see a single soul the entire time. Frank, you mentioned seeing Bob head into medbay from electrical around tick 8. Depending on exactly when I passed through medbay and electrical, it's possible we just missed each other, but the fact remains I didn't encounter him or anyone else.\n\nGiven Diana found the body in security and Frank caught Bob leaving that exact corridor, Bob is absolutely the prime suspect here. Bob, you're the last one to speak, so the floor is yours. You really need to explain what you were doing near security and why you left. Unless you have an incredibly solid alibi or can point out a flaw in Frank's timeline, I think we have our duck. I'll listen to your defense, but I'm leaning heavily towards voting you right now."}}
{"timestamp": 1779339496.8547287, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "Frank is absolutely right, I *did* come from the Security corridor at tick 8, but if you look at the timeline, that actually clears me! \n\nI started near Weapons and saw Eve there around ticks 2 and 3. At tick 4, she moved down to Security. I popped my head into Security at tick 5, saw she was perfectly fine and doing her tasks, and then I immediately headed left towards Electrical and Medbay\u2014which is exactly when Frank saw me. \n\nThink about the timing here, guys. The meeting was called at tick 19. If I had killed her right before Frank saw me, her body would have just been sitting there for over 10 ticks. Diana, you just said you arrived in Security at the very end of a massive route across the entire map, and you found the right side completely empty. If I left at tick 8, the killer had plenty of time to slip into Security, kill her, and leave through Navigation or vent away while the right side was empty. \n\nAlice, you were down in Navigation, are you absolutely sure nobody slipped past you? And Charlie, you traversed the entire bottom half of the map and didn't see a single soul? That feels incredibly convenient. \n\nI swear on my feathers I left Eve alive. Voting me out because I was honest about being in the same time zone as her early in the game is exactly what the real Duck wants. I'm skipping because we don't have hard proof on who went into Security *after* I left, but you guys need to look harder at Alice or Charlie.\n\n=== VOTE ===\nskip"}}
