{"timestamp": 1779339559.3231134, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 19, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I need everyone to slow down and look at the actual timeline before you make a huge mistake. Yes, Frank, you saw me come from the Security corridor at tick 8, and I won't deny that. But let's look at the facts: the meeting was called at tick 19! \n\nI was with Eve early on; I saw her in Weapons around ticks 2 and 3, and then I popped into Security at tick 5. She was perfectly fine, doing her tasks. I left her alive and immediately headed left toward Electrical and Medbay, which perfectly lines up with Frank seeing me at tick 8. \n\nThat means there were 11 whole ticks between when I left Security and when this meeting was called. 11 ticks! Diana even said that when she finally arrived at Security at the end of her massive route, the right side of the ship was completely empty. The killer had plenty of time to slip into Security after I was already gone, take out Eve, and escape through Navigation or vent away. \n\nCharlie, you traversed the entire bottom half of the map and claim you didn't see a single soul the whole time? That is incredibly convenient. The killer definitely slipped in from the bottom right after I left. Voting me out because I was honest about being near Eve early in the game is exactly what the real Duck wants you to do. I am voting Charlie because his empty route is highly suspicious.\n\nCharlie"}}
